.TH MDB2REC "1" "April 2026" "GNU recutils 1.9.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdb2rec \- mdb to rec converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdb2rec
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]... \fI\,MDB_FILE \/\fR[\fI\,TABLE\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert an mdb file into a rec file.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-system\-tables\fR
include system tables.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-empty\-fields\fR
don't prune empty fields in the rec
output.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-tables\fR
dump a list of the table names contained
in the mdb file.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
List available tables in an MDB file:

  mdb2rec --list-tables database.mdb

Convert a specific table to rec format:

  mdb2rec -t Employees database.mdb > employees.rec

Convert all tables:

  mdb2rec database.mdb > all.rec
